# Game regressions

The user requests all four fixes under docs/README.md and its linked requirements. They require a plan first, each implementation task assigned to its own subagent, and no code edits by the primary agent.

Plan: separate agents restore best-score minimums and the absent label; arrow navigation and focus behavior; reduced-motion CSS; silence without removing announcements. Run targeted checks for each and the full required checks after integration. Only one subagent can run alongside the primary agent.

Observed causes: rememberBest always replaces; GameStatus uses zero for missing bests; Board has no arrow handler; card and status styles lack reduced-motion overrides; use-game creates tones for matches and wins.

Score fix delegated task 1 to `/root/best_scores`: `rememberBest` now keeps the existing score for equal or worse results, and `GameStatus` shows `none` when a size lacks a record. Existing storage/session and browser tests cover comparisons, per-size persistence and missing bests. Focused storage/session tests pass (17 tests). Primary agent coordinates remaining tasks and runs full verification. Git commands need `git -c safe.directory=/work`.

